menu "Michi Music Stream Time"

    comment "SNTP wall clock for signed discovery (P0-02): the signed announce carries a timestamp that Michi Link rejects outside +-90 s. Requires CONFIG_LWIP_SNTP=y (set in sdkconfig.defaults)."

    config MICHI_TIME_SNTP_SERVER
        string "SNTP server hostname"
        default "pool.ntp.org"
        help
          NTP server used by the esp_netif SNTP client (one server,
          the standard public pool). Nothing sensitive - the firmware
          only queries it.

    config MICHI_TIME_SYNC_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "SNTP sync wait timeout per attempt (ms)"
        default 10000
        range 1000 60000
        help
          Bound of ONE esp_netif_sntp_sync_wait round in the dedicated
          sync task. The wait never runs on the esp_event task: GOT_IP
          handlers stay non-blocking (P0-11). On timeout the task
          restarts the SNTP client and retries (see
          MICHI_TIME_SYNC_RETRIES).

    config MICHI_TIME_SYNC_RETRIES
        int "SNTP sync attempts per network up"
        default 2
        range 1 10
        help
          How many bounded sync_wait rounds the sync task runs after
          each network-up before giving up for that round. Exhaustion
          conserves the last synchronized state (documented policy in
          michi_time.h) - it never flips a previously synchronized
          device back to unsynchronized.

    config MICHI_TIME_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Time sync task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 8192
        help
          Stack of the "michi_time_sync" task (priority 2). It blocks
          on semaphores almost forever and only runs the bounded
          sync_wait rounds plus a few flag stores per sync event.

endmenu
